---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/contact';
import { RETENTION_DAYS } from '../lib/contact-form';
import { UMAMI_HOST_URL, UMAMI_RETENTION_MONTHS } from '../lib/analytics';

/*
 * The privacy policy, which specification.website grades Required.
 *
 * IT IS SHORT BECAUSE THE ANSWER IS SHORT. This is a static site on a
 * Cloudflare Worker with no accounts, and its one piece of server-side code
 * is the contact form, which stores what is sent in D1. It sets no cookies,
 * writes to no storage API and loads nothing from a third-party origin: the
 * fonts and the analytics script are served from this domain and the built
 * output has no external subresource. The one thing a page sends elsewhere is
 * the visit count to Umami, which has its own section.
 *
 * EVERY CLAIM ON THIS PAGE IS TESTED. A privacy policy is the easiest
 * document on a site to make quietly false: it is written once, and then an
 * embed, a CDN font or a hit counter is added and nothing notices the page
 * still says otherwise. tests/privacy.spec.ts asserts each claim against the
 * source and the build, naming the sentence that has stopped being true.
 * tests/analytics.spec.ts does the same for the "Visit counts" section,
 * against what the tracker really sends.
 *
 * WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CLAIMED: anything about Cloudflare's own logging.
 * Serving this site means Cloudflare receives the requests, and what they
 * retain is their policy rather than ours, so "we log nothing" would read as
 * "nothing is logged". The page says what is true and points at their policy.
 *
 * THE COPY IS FACTUAL DISCLOSURE, NOT EDITORIAL. Every sentence describes
 * verifiable behaviour of the software, which is the line AGENTS.md draws.
 * The wording is still worth Sinduri reading, because a privacy policy is a
 * promise made on her behalf.
 */

/*
 * The build date, not a date this page maintains. The page is rebuilt on
 * every deploy, and a hand-written date would drift from the content it is
 * meant to date.
 */
const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);

const HOST = 'sinduri.lol';
const CLOUDFLARE_PRIVACY = 'https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/';
const UMAMI_PRIVACY = 'https://umami.is/privacy';
const UMAMI_HOST = new URL(UMAMI_HOST_URL).host;

/*
 * How long Cloudflare keeps Workers logs and traces on the Free plan, set by
 * the platform rather than by wrangler.jsonc. A plan change changes it.
 */
const WORKER_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS = 3;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | sinduri.lol"
  description="This site sets no cookies, loads nothing from anywhere else, and counts visits with cookie-free analytics."
>
  <section class="band py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-page">
      <h1 class="text-h1 text-gold">Privacy</h1>

      <p class="mt-10 max-w-prose text-h3 font-bold text-text text-pretty">
        This site sets no cookies and loads nothing from any other domain. It
        counts visits with Umami, which does not use cookies either. The only
        thing it stores about you is what you type into the contact form, and
        only so that there is something to reply to.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{lastUpdated}</time>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-page">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-gold">What this site does not do</h2>

      <ul class="mt-10 max-w-prose list-disc pl-6 text-muted marker:text-gold">
        <li class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-text">No cookies.</strong> Nothing on {HOST} sets
          a cookie, and nothing reads one.
        </li>
        <li class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-text">No browser storage.</strong> Nothing is
          written to local storage, session storage or a database in your
          browser. The analytics script reads one local storage setting, named
          umami.disabled, which is Umami's own off switch, and writes nothing.
        </li>
        <li class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-text">Nothing loaded from other domains.</strong>
          Every file a page loads comes from this domain: the fonts, the images
          and the analytics script. There are no embeds, no tag manager and no
          advertising. The site's own security policy blocks anything off-domain
          from loading at all.
        </li>
        <li class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-text">No accounts.</strong> There is nothing to
          sign up for and nothing to log in to. The contact form is the only
          thing on this site that stores anything, and what it stores is below.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-page">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-gold">Visit counts</h2>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        This site counts visits with{' '}
        <a
          href="https://umami.is/"
          class="underline decoration-gold underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan"
        >
          Umami
        </a>
        , an analytics service that uses no cookies and does not follow you from
        site to site. The script runs from this domain, and what it sends goes
        to Umami at {UMAMI_HOST}, which stores it on servers in the European
        Union and keeps it for {UMAMI_RETENTION_MONTHS} months. It is the only
        place a page here sends anything to.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        For each page you open, it sends the page's address and title, the
        address of the page that linked you here if your browser shares it, your
        screen size and your browser's language.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        When you click a link or a button, it also sends what kind of control it
        was, its label, which part of the page it is in and, for a link, where
        it goes. For an email link the address is left out. Nothing you type is
        ever sent, including what you write in the contact form.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        Like any server, Umami receives your IP address and your browser's
        details with each request. Umami says it uses the IP address to work out
        your country, region and city, and your browser details to work out your
        browser, operating system and type of device, and that it does not store
        the IP address. How Umami handles that is covered by{' '}
        <a
          href={UMAMI_PRIVACY}
          class="underline decoration-gold underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan"
        >
          Umami's privacy policy
        </a>
        .
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        If your browser sends Do Not Track, nothing is sent at all. Blocking
        JavaScript for this site stops it too.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-20 text-h2 text-gold">Links away from here</h2>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        The footer links to profiles on other sites, and posts may link
        elsewhere. Those are ordinary links: nothing is sent when the page
        loads, only when you follow one. Once you do, that site's own policy
        applies and this one does not.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-20 text-h2 text-gold">Hosting</h2>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        This site is served by a Cloudflare Worker. Delivering a page means
        Cloudflare receives the request for it, including your IP address, in
        the same way any web server does. What they keep, and for how long, is
        covered by{' '}
        <a
          href={CLOUDFLARE_PRIVACY}
          class="underline decoration-gold underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan"
        >
          Cloudflare's privacy policy
        </a>{' '}
        rather than by this one.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        Requests that run this site's own code, which in practice means sending
        the contact form, are also logged to this site's Cloudflare account so
        that problems can be fixed. A log entry holds the request and response,
        which can include your IP address, and your browser and approximate
        location: city, country and network provider. Logs are deleted
        automatically after {WORKER_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS} days and are not stored
        with your message. Loading a page in a browser is not logged this way.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-20 text-h2 text-gold">The contact form</h2>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        The form on <a href="/contact/">the contact page</a> stores the name,
        email address and message you type, so that there is something to reply
        to. Nothing else is recorded with it: no IP address, no browser, no
        referrer, and no identifier of any kind. It is stored in a database
        restricted to the European Union, and a copy is emailed to the site
        owner's inbox, which is hosted by Google, so that the message is seen
        and can be answered.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        To stop the form being used for bulk submissions, the number of
        submissions from one network address is limited. That check reads your
        address, hashes it together with the current date, and keeps only the
        hash for as long as the limit runs. The check does not write the address
        down, and the hash is not stored with your message or linked to it.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        Messages are deleted from the database after {RETENTION_DAYS} days. The
        emailed copy is kept like any other email, for as long as it is needed
        to reply. To have both removed sooner, write to{' '}
        <a
          href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}
          class="underline decoration-gold underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan"
        >
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>{' '}
        and say so; you do not need to give a reason.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-20 text-h2 text-gold">Email</h2>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        If you write to{' '}
        <a
          href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}
          class="underline decoration-gold underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan"
        >
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>
        , that message is kept in order to reply to it. It is not added to any
        list and it is not passed on.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-20 text-h2 text-gold">Questions</h2>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-muted text-pretty">
        Ask at{' '}
        <a
          href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}
          class="underline decoration-gold underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan"
        >
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
